wikitext.Dahmen, Johan Arnold:
{{#fte:person
|Birth Date=1766 March or February?
|Death Date=3/4 September 1812
|Time Period=Classical
|Nationality=Dutch
|Sex=male
|Biography Link={{wp|nl:Johan Arnold Dahmen (1766-1812)|Dutch}} ; possibly {{plain|http://www.dbnl.org/tekst/aa__001biog05_01/aa__001biog05_01_0022.php|Biographisch woordenboek der Nederlanden, deel 4}}.  Johan Arnold Dahmen (he often anglicised it to John Arnold Dahmen) was part of a large musical family (Wilhelm Dahmen was the father).  He is not to be confused with Arnoldus Dahmen (1768-1829), his younger brother and a flautist, who settled in Amsterdam; <span class="plainlinks">[http://books.google.com/books?id=fM09AAAAcAAJ&pg=PA235 Fétis, 1836]</span>
|Alternative Names=Johann Arnold, Jean Arnold, Jean André, Johann Arnoldus
|List Pages=*{{ms|100020064}}
*{{viaf|4728419}}
|Extra Information=*Baptised 9 March 1766. Seems to have been traditional then but not universal to baptise people within a month of birth (when possible). Born in the Hague, died in London in early September (either 3rd or 4th) 1812, and buried in the church-yard of St. Andrew Undershaft, St. Mary Axe on 5 September 1812. Some sources have "JA Dahmen (1766{{EN}}1813)." (e.g. Cowgill, Holman ''Music in the British provinces, 1690-1914'' page 186.).  New Grove, and other sources, erroneously give Dahmen's death as 1794. (There were at least two Johan Arnold Dahmens: one a harpist, one a cellist; this was the cellist, who was the uncle of the harpist.)  
}}

